---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Shanghai Travel Guide: The Most Foreigner-Friendly City";
const description = "Shanghai guide — attractions, food, transport, and where to stay in China's most international city.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🏙️ Shanghai</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">Shanghai Travel Guide: The Most Foreigner-Friendly City</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Shanghai guide — attractions, food, transport, and where to stay in China's most international city.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 7 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-yellow-50 to-amber-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-4">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-yellow-800 leading-relaxed">Shanghai is <strong>China's most foreigner-friendly city</strong>. It has the largest English-speaking population, the most international restaurants, and a skyline that rivals any in the world. If you're nervous about the language barrier or culture shock, Shanghai is the gentlest introduction to China.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#why-visit" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🌆 Why Visit Shanghai?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-many-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#attractions" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎯 Top Attractions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#getting-around" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚇 Getting Around</a></li>
        <li><a href="#where-to-stay" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏨 Where to Stay</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-to-eat" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🍜 What to Eat</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="why-visit" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🌆 Why Visit Shanghai?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">Shanghai feels like a city of the future. The Pudong skyline — with the Oriental Pearl Tower and Shanghai Tower piercing the clouds — is the face of modern China. But the old city still has charm: the French Concession's tree-lined streets, the art deco buildings along the Bund, and the winding lanes of Old Town. Shanghai is also a food lover's paradise, with some of the best fine dining in Asia alongside street stalls serving soup dumplings that will change your life.</p>

    <h2 id="how-many-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>3 days (standard):</strong> The Bund, Old Town, French Concession, and a skyline visit</li>
      <li><strong>4–5 days (comfortable):</strong> Add Disneyland, Zhujiajiao Water Town, or a two-day trip to Suzhou</li>
      <li><strong>5+ days (deep dive):</strong> Explore the city's museums, art galleries, and nightlife neighborhoods in depth</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="attractions" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🎯 Top Attractions</h2>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">The Bund (外滩)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">Shanghai's iconic waterfront promenade is lined with colonial-era buildings on one side and the Pudong skyscrapers on the other. Best visited at sunset when the lights come on.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Shanghai Tower (上海中心大厦)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">China's tallest building and the third tallest in the world. The observation deck at 546 meters gives you a view over all of Shanghai. The elevator ride is an experience in itself — it reaches 20 m/s.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Yu Garden (豫园)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">A 400-year-old Ming dynasty garden hidden in the heart of Old Town. Surrounded by the Yuyuan Bazaar, a lively market area full of snacks and souvenirs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">French Concession (法租界)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">Once the French colonial district, now the trendiest part of Shanghai. Wukang Road and Anfu Road are perfect for café hopping, boutique shopping, and people-watching.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Zhujiajiao Water Town (朱家角)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">An ancient water town just 45 minutes from downtown Shanghai. Canals, stone bridges, and Ming-era buildings. A half-day trip that feels a world away from the city skyscrapers.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="getting-around" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🚇 Getting Around</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Subway:</strong> Shanghai has the longest metro system in the world (19 lines, 800+ km). Everything is labeled in English. Check the <a href="/en/transport/metro-bus/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Metro & Bus Guide for Major Chinese Cities</a> for route tips.</li>
      <li><strong>Didi:</strong> Works perfectly. Use it for short trips or when the subway doesn't go there. Get setup tips in <a href="/en/transport/didi/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Use Didi in China as a Foreigner</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Maglev (磁悬浮):</strong> The world's fastest commercial train, connecting Pudong Airport to downtown (7 minutes, 430 km/h). Worth doing for the experience.</li>
      <li><strong>Biking:</strong> Shanghai is flat and bike-friendly. Shared bikes are everywhere in the city center.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="where-to-stay" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🏨 Where to Stay</h2>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">The Bund / Lujiazui (外滩/陆家嘴) — Best for first-time visitors</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Iconic views, close to major attractions, plenty of luxury hotels. Pricier but worth the splurge.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">French Concession (法租界) — Best for foodies and culture lovers</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The trendiest area with great restaurants, bars, and boutiques. Quiet streets lined with plane trees.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Jing'an (静安) — Best for shopping and nightlife</h3><p class="text-gray-700">A vibrant commercial district with excellent metro connections. Close to Nanjing Road and Jing'an Temple.</p></div>

    <h2 id="what-to-eat" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🍜 What to Eat</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Xiaolongbao (小笼包)</strong> — Soup dumplings filled with pork and broth that explode in your mouth. The ultimate Shanghai food experience.</li>
      <li><strong>Shengjianbao (生煎包)</strong> — Pan-fried pork buns with a crispy bottom and juicy filling.</li>
      <li><strong>Red Braised Pork — Hong Shao Rou (红烧肉)</strong> — Pork belly slow-cooked in soy sauce and sugar until melt-in-your-mouth tender.</li>
      <li><strong>Scallion Oil Noodles — Cong You Ban Mian (葱油拌面)</strong> — Simple but addictive noodles in scallion-infused oil.</li>
      <li><strong>Crab — Da Zha Xie (大闸蟹)</strong> — In autumn, hairy crabs from nearby Yangcheng Lake are a Shanghai obsession.</li>
      <li><strong>Lao Shanghai Milk Tea (老上海奶茶)</strong> — A nostalgic powdered milk-and-tea drink locals grew up with.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="not-prose mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">📚 Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <a href="/en/cities/city-select/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🗺️ <strong>How Many Days in China?</strong> — Plan your full itinerary</a>
        <a href="/en/cities/beijing-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🏛️ <strong>Beijing Travel Guide</strong> — See how Shanghai compares</a>
        <a href="/en/transport/metro-bus/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🚇 <strong>Metro & Bus Guide for Major Chinese Cities</strong> — Navigate Shanghai's subway</a>
        <a href="/en/payment/payment-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">💳 <strong>How to Pay in China</strong> — Alipay and WeChat Pay setup</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>